ui-center-a-modal-time-picker-above-a-scrim-the-main-content-remains-visible-for-context-but = Center a modal time picker above a scrim. The main content remains visible for context but is unavailable until the picker closes. Keep the whole container, input-mode switch and confirmation actions on screen.

ui-use-the-dialog-below-to-try-a-real-modal-changes-remain-a-draft-until-ok-cancel-or-a-click = Use the dialog below to try a real modal. Changes remain a draft until OK; Cancel or a click outside the dialog preserves the saved value.

ui-offer-both-touch-and-keyboard-entry-people-using-a-screen-reader-a-physical-keyboard-or-an = Offer both touch and keyboard entry. People using a screen reader, a physical keyboard or an alternative input device must be able to set a time without dragging a clock hand. Respect the person's 12- or 24-hour format preference.

ui-accessible-input = Accessible input

ui-always-expose-manual-time-entry-through-the-keyboard-icon-on-the-dial-a-clock-icon-returns = Always expose manual time entry through the keyboard icon on the dial. A clock icon returns to dial selection. Prefer the input variant when a dial is unnecessary or the available screen cannot contain it comfortably.

ui-dial-selection-targets-are-48-48dp-the-annotated-illustrations-may-scale-to-fit-this-artic = Dial selection targets are 48 × 48dp. The annotated illustrations may scale to fit this article; production controls should retain their interactive target sizes rather than shrinking the dial to fit.

ui-focus-and-selection = Focus and selection

ui-keep-a-visible-focus-indicator-as-well-as-selected-colors-hour-and-minute-supporting-label = Keep a visible focus indicator as well as selected colors. Hour and Minute supporting labels identify editable fields; AM and PM expose their selected state. Moving focus to a dial value does not confirm the time.

